  subgraph env["One uv-managed venv — one Python, ordinary Python package deps only;\nthe same on both floors: Linux + NVIDIA and Apple Silicon"]
    app["Stream\n(stream.py: @stream functions over a Stream builder compile the stream's graph\nfrom @node classes — today's app; hosts no node; may expose ports; one venv installs the\npure-Python stream package; the graph is data — one shape with what the\nruntime renders live — that a runtime runs) — decided, not yet built"]
    procs["Node classes\n(importable modules — imported by the stream,\nregistering their descriptor as the decorator runs, run by processor interpreters;\nnever hosted in the stream's process or the runtime process;\nthe class's import path is its identity)"]
    pkgs["Extension wheels\n(ordinary PyPI packages — Rust inside for speed, a Python processor\nas the binding; depend on the streamlib wheel as a binary, never link the engine;\nnative internals expose handles, never streamlib internals;\ntwo mechanisms — a processor extension added by rt.add that calls its own\nRust directly, and a capability extension: support code declared by a pyproject\nentry point pip records, run once at startup like a driver, sandboxed, able to\nintroduce engine-grade capabilities the engine does not provide; first-party optional capabilities ship this way too,\nnetworking shipped first — streamlib-webrtc (WhipPublisher / WhepPlayer) and\nstreamlib-moq (MoqBroadcastPublisher / MoqBroadcastSubscriber), both on the encoded\nside of the codec blocks, touching no surface and no GPU;\nthe MoQ pair also carries data tracks under streamlib_bag — any bag as a track\nbeside video and audio, named by track_names, the producer's stamp intact,\na late media bag shed and its backlogged group abandoned on the vendored moq-transport;\ngraph carries what loaded as its extensions key;\nlive in packages/, local-linked in-repo,\npublished via the wheel's multi-project index;\ndecided, not yet built: renamed tatolab-moq / tatolab-webrtc, importing as\ntatolab.moq / tatolab.webrtc and depending on tatolab-stream; the capability-extension\nhook deleted — no package extends the engine, each sets itself up where its nodes run)"]
    wheel["streamlib wheel\n(Python API + CLI + engine, PyO3 — repo releases now, PyPI after rename;\nbecomes two distributions under a tatolab.* namespace (decided): the pure-Python\ntatolab-stream (tatolab.stream) every stream venv installs and compiles with, no runtime\npresent; and the native tatolab.runtime shipped only with the runtime, lent to each\nprocessor interpreter on PYTHONPATH — a venv holds no engine, and the runtime refuses\nby name what it does not understand in a graph — with no streamlib-owned service\n(decided, not yet built);\none manylinux wheel and one aarch64-apple-darwin wheel — the macOS one\ncarrying the Vulkan loader and MoltenVK, named to the loader additively;\none _engine.pyi gated by stubtest against both binaries, so the two floors\nare one surface and an absent capability is a closed list refused by name;\nits bag codec is exported as the one encode/decode pair\nan extension carrying a bag over its own transport reaches)"]
    helper["Processor interpreters — every Python node\n(engine exec of sys.executable; own\ninterpreter, own GIL; imports the wheel —\nand refuses to start unless that wheel is the\nparent's own engine build, id checked before\nany channel or socket opens;\nthe only placement;\ndecided, not yet built: exec'd from the stream's own venv interpreter with the\nruntime's lend directory (holding tatolab/runtime/) prepended to PYTHONPATH, so the child\nimports the lent tatolab.runtime beside the venv's tatolab.stream — a venv holds no engine)"]
  end

  rustapp["Rust app\n(plain cargo project)"]
  crate["streamlib crate\n(embeddable Rust library)"]
  engine["Engine runtime\n(runtime/streamlib-engine;\none runtime per machine runs many streams (decided, not yet built):\ntatolabd, owned by one user — another user's runtime is refused; one GpuContext,\nZenoh session, local API and relay per machine; event topic, registry, interpreter,\nlogs, shutdown and interpreter table per stream; streams link freely on the machine;\nrun / run -d (kept, re-loaded on start) / stop / streams / dev; on Apple, an\nSMAppService agent inside Tatolab.app)"]
  media["Built-in media blocks\n(camera / display / MicrophoneSource / SpeakerSink — native,\nin the wheel, handle-shaped primitives;\ncapture on one video device seam — V4L2 on Linux, AVFoundation on Apple —\neach frame carrying its capture instant on both stamps, a future stamp clamped and counted;\nthe Apple event pump on the process's first thread, present from a CAMetalLayer;\naudio backend per platform — CoreAudio AUHAL → null on Apple; on Linux dlopen'd: PipeWire → ALSA → null,\nchosen by opening not by loading; vendored SPA headers\ncompile to a shim that calls only pointers, so no audio\nlibrary enters DT_NEEDED;\ndevice-paced, conditioning on the built-ins;\ncodec blocks: H264/H265 encode+decode on one video codec backend seam —\nVulkan Video on Linux, VideoToolbox on Apple, one Annex-B wire on both —\none encode body and one decode body specialised by codec identity,\ncolour conversion on the engine's existing rgb_to_nv12 — no new RHI primitive;\nall four reach Python as marker classes like every other built-in, and the\nencoded frame has a Python cast (EncodedVideoFrame) holding no surface;\nOpus encode+decode shipped over statically linked libopus, and a pure-Rust\nfragmented Mp4Sink muxing both on every platform — one track per inbound link, named by its channel;\nJpegDecoder frozen until its drone consumer returns, and the next codec\nfollows the built-in criterion rather than joining this node — an encoded frame is an\nordinary bag, bitstream inline as bin beside the ordering pair and sync-point flag;\nan encoded audio packet is that convention applied to audio, cast by EncodedAudioPacket;\na decoder publishes the SPS display window, never the padded coded picture;\nVirtualCameraSink (Linux only; no Apple port — a Camera Extension needs a bundle): one camera per processor, created at setup and removed at teardown,\nthat any other application on the machine opens — built-in under criterion (c),\ntwo doors chosen at setup and logged: a v4l2loopback device it creates through the\nmodule's control node, YUYV written by one GPU pass through the RHI's host-pointer\nimport (cached-staging copy where the driver refuses it, imported on the rig), else a\nPipeWire Video/Source node with media.role = Camera over the same dlsym'd shim, whose\nvideo half shares the audio half's entry-point list; the loopback permission is a\none-time enable-virtual-camera the user runs, never elevated by the engine)"]
  rhi["RHI\n(accelerators optional — a stream that needs no GPU runs on a machine\nwithout one (decided, not yet built);\nvulkan/rhi + streamlib-consumer-rhi —\nthe one Vulkan RHI on both floors, MoltenVK the macOS driver;\nMetal only as handles exported from Vulkan objects;\na driver's missing capability is an absent tier refused by name)"]
  interop["Interop adapters\n(app-process Rust, per floor — Vulkan, cpu-readback, skia on both;\nVulkan↔GL and Vulkan↔CUDA on Linux, named absent on macOS)"]
  ctl["Control plane\n(api-server: HTTP / WS / MCP — engine-side;\nserves the processor catalog — every registered type with its derived\nconfig schema and ports — the live graph, and recipes over its tools;\ndecided, not yet built: one local API per machine, served by the runtime on a socket\nonly the owning user can open — no network address serves control, and another\nmachine's streams are changed on that machine (ssh) or by the control client;\nMCP hosts launch the CLI's mcp verb, a stdio forwarder to the socket (ssh for another\nmachine), and the runtime serves only MCP's current stateless revision, 2026-07-28;\nevery exposed port reachable by URL from any tool in the form that tool wants, on a\nseparate read-only listener, loopback by default, LAN or tailnet on request)"]
  cli["CLI — today in the wheel\nnew / dev / run · nodes / graph / tap / logs / exchange · enable-virtual-camera\n(new scaffolds a GlslPixelEffect plus a numpy meter; dev / run print the\ncross-floor check's warnings and never block a start;\ndecided, not yet built: the native tatolab beside tatolabd, shipped with the runtime\nby the installer and never on pip — run / run -d / stop / streams / dev, and the mcp verb)"]
  wire["Wire\n(self-describing bags between nodes —\nthe only cross-language boundary)"]

  registry["Node registry\n(one JSON per live node, inside the one engine-resolved runtime\ndirectory — on Linux XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/streamlib where that is set and non-empty,\notherwise, and on macOS always, /tmp/streamlib-<uid>, owner-only and checked\nbefore the first write — which also holds the\nsurface socket and the engine-owned iceoryx2 domain)"]
  mesh["Runtime mesh (Zenoh) — decided, not yet built:\none session per machine, the machine's single Zenoh router, built from the runtime's\nown configuration and dialing routers; a pushed stream map refuses links to unexposed\nports and authenticates peers; the relay is a role of the same runtime software, dialed\nwhere machines cannot reach each other; MoQ only as a browser form, never a link between\nruntimes; NAT, peer identity and wire encryption left to Tailscale, a VPN or a relay.\nShipped today (superseded where the decided shape says otherwise):\nengine transport, always on, beside iceoryx2 — one session per runtime, closed at stop(),\nnever in a processor interpreter, and opened from engine defaults (superseded: the runtime's own configuration);\na runtime announces itself with a liveliness token plus a description queryable and\ndiscovers peers peer-to-peer, explicit peers or a router where multicast\ndoes not cross; a session that cannot bind runs local-only and says why once;\neverything under a mesh name, default `default`;\nports addressed runtime name / display name / port (a stream level is OPEN), the runtime\nname unique in the mesh, host identity the boot id and pid namespace on Linux, the boot session on Apple;\na remote link is spelled in Python as rt.remote_processor_output / _input and over MCP as a\nruntime name plus a display name on either end of connect — today any runtime may wire it\n(superseded: the stream map decides what leaves a machine);\nthe input's runtime always applies it, with connect's own refusals, so a push and a\nthird-party wiring are one link request — a Zenoh query kept and resent while that\nruntime is absent or silent, idempotent on the link_request_id the link carries;\na link waits as awaiting_remote with a reason and wires itself when the reason clears,\na missing port is refused listing what is offered, and a port the source stopped\nsending says why in the source's own words and that nothing is retrying it;\nnothing is sent for a port no remote link reads — the first reader makes one egress\non its own thread, the last reader's leave removes it, and one ingress per source\nwrites into an engine-named local channel as its single publisher;\nstamps cross unchanged, every link naming the machine whose monotonic clock they\nwere taken on, never compared across machines (a shared network clock is OPEN);\na send the network cannot take is dropped, and every bag lost on the hop is counted\nper remote link from the sequence number the attachment carries end to end;\nnotify, event bus, request-response and blackboard never cross;\ngraph lists mesh peers, the ports other runtimes are reading and the requests still\nwaiting; a top-level surface_id crosses as pixels and lands as a fresh\nlocal surface id; no authentication shipped (superseded: the stream map and peer authentication)"]

  ctlclient["External control client\n(decided, not yet built: an extension point —\nstreamlib runs complete without one; how it plugs in is OPEN —\ndirection: an entry point with a role of its own, or another seam)"]
